{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.minimal_z5_classification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.minimal_z5_classification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.minimal_z5_classification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.minimal_z5_classification","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/minimal_z5_classification.lean#L37-L57","doc":"**Minimal `ℤ₅`-hyperelliptic classification** (Riemann–Hurwitz\nnumerics) — [manuscript theorem].\n\nLet `X` be a smooth projective Riemann surface of minimal genus that is\nhyperelliptic (degree-`2` cover `π : X → ℙ¹` with involution `ι`) and\nadmits a faithful `ℤ₅` automorphism `φ` commuting with `ι`.  The\nmanuscript shows by the `bar φ`-orbit / Möbius-normalisation argument\nthat the minimal such genus is `g = 2`; this is the lone open geometric\ninput, carried as the hypothesis `hg : g = 2`.\n\nGiven `g = 2`, the branch-divisor cardinality is **derived**:\n`|Branch(π)| = 2g + 2 = 6`.  (The full classification — `X ≅ 𝒳₅ :\ny² = x⁵ − 1` — concerns the curve isomorphism and is tracked\nseparately.) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:hyperelliptic-z5-classification","label":"thm:hyperelliptic-z5-classification","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/hyperelliptic-z5-classification.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.branchCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.branchCount","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/minimal_z5_classification.lean#L33-L35","doc":"Riemann–Hurwitz branch count for a hyperelliptic (degree-`2`)\ncover: `|Branch(π)| = 2g + 2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}